 side of the equation:\n\\[ 12 - y - 6 = y - 12, \\]\n\\[ 6 - y = y - 12. \\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\( y \\) by isolating it on one side of the equation. First, add \\( y \\) to both sides:\n\\[ 6 = 2y - 12. \\]\n\nThen, add 12 to both sides:\n\\[ 18 = 2y. \\]\n\nFinally, divide both sides by 2:\n\\[ y = 9. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( y \\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:911"}
